-Regenerate NGAP/S1AP ASN.1 files
-================================
+Regenerate NGAP/S1AP/CHF-CDR ASN.1 files
+========================================
 
 This document describes how to regenerate the NGAP/S1AP ASN.1
 encoder/decoder files for Open5GS using `asn1c`.
@@ -7,6 +7,12 @@ encoder/decoder files for Open5GS using `asn1c`.
 The generated files are based on the 3GPP ASN.1 specifications and the
 `mouse07410/asn1c` `vlm_master` branch.
 
+There is a third bundle, `cdr-r19.6.0/`, holding the TS 32.298 CHF CDR
+records. It uses the same `asn1c` at the same commit, but its input is
+assembled by a script rather than prepared by hand, and it is generated for
+BER rather than APER. See "Regenerate the CHF CDR ASN.1 files" below; the
+NGAP/S1AP steps in between do not apply to it.
+
 Use mouse07410/vlm_master asn1c
 ===============================
 
@@ -292,6 +298,109 @@ rm -f \
     pdu_collection.c
 ```
 
+Regenerate the CHF CDR ASN.1 files
+==================================
+
+The CHF charging records in `lib/asn1c/cdr/` come from
+`lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/`. Unlike S1AP and NGAP there is no hand-made
+input file to prepare: `generator.sh` assembles the module, runs `asn1c` and
+cleans up after it.
+
+The ASN.1 is not in the specification
+-------------------------------------
+
+TS 32.298 Rel-19 clause 5.2.5 says only that the ASN.1 definitions are
+specified in 3GPP Forge, so there is no `.txt` to extract from a `.doc` as
+there is for S1AP and NGAP. `standard/` holds `TS32298_CHFChargingDataTypes.asn`
+and its two dependencies, taken verbatim from Forge:
+
+```text
+https://forge.3gpp.org/rep/sa5/CH   branch Rel-19, directory ASN
+commit 3e24b9aa
+```
+
+Do not edit anything in `standard/`. Corrections and trims live in
+`patched/`, which is the only hand-written ASN.1 in the bundle:
+
+```text
+standard/        pristine 3GPP, exactly as published
+patched/         chf-5gsa-records.asn  - the records trimmed to the 5G SA path
+                 spec-defects.asn      - corrections for defects in the published module
+closure.py       standard + patched -> modified/
+modified/        the asn1c input, committed so a reviewer can read it
+generator.sh     modified/ -> lib/asn1c/cdr/
+```
+
+`patched/spec-defects.asn` currently carries one entry: the published
+`NetworkFunctionality` is missing the comma after `aIOTF (23)`, so the
+`ENUMERATED` does not parse and the module will not compile as published. The
+corrected definition is copied verbatim apart from that comma. Check whether
+it is still needed on a release bump, and delete it when 3GPP fixes it.
+
+Run the generator
+-----------------
+
+```sh
+cd ~/Documents/git/open5gs/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0
+
+ASN1C=~/Documents/git/my/asn1c/asn1c/asn1c ./generator.sh
+```
+
+It prints the number of `.c` and `.h` files written, and warns if any skeleton
+it copied differs from `lib/asn1c/common`'s — check whether that is an `asn1c`
+version difference before committing it.
+
+BER, not APER
+-------------
+
+TS 32.298 clause 6.1 requires BER on the Bx interface, which is the mirror
+image of S1AP and NGAP: those are generated with `-no-gen-BER` and keep APER,
+and the CDR codec keeps BER and drops APER. `asn1c` writes that choice into
+`asn_config.h`.
+
+That is why `lib/asn1c/cdr/` keeps its own full copy of the `asn1c` runtime
+instead of sharing `lib/asn1c/common/`. A C quote-include resolves against the
+including file's own directory first, so sharing `common`'s sources would
+compile them against `common`'s BER-disabled `asn_config.h` while the generated
+code used the BER-enabled one — and the two disagree about the layout of
+`asn_TYPE_operation_s`. That mismatch links cleanly and fails at run time, so
+the duplication is deliberate. `generator.sh` copies the Open5GS-patched
+`asn_internal.h` from `common` rather than re-deriving the allocator patch
+described under "Check common ASN.1 runtime file", and refuses to run if
+`common`'s copy is not the patched one.
+
+Update generated source/header lists
+------------------------------------
+
+Neither `lib/asn1c/cdr/meson.build` nor `lib/asn1c/cdr/ogs-asn1c-cdr.h` is
+generated, and both are synced by hand. The `Makefile.am.libasncodec` method
+used for NGAP/S1AP above is not available here, because `generator.sh` deletes
+that file along with the other fragments `asn1c` leaves behind. List the files
+directly instead:
+
+```sh
+cd ~/Documents/git/open5gs/lib/asn1c/cdr
+
+ls *.c | sort | sed "s|^|    |"
+ls CHFCDR_*.h | sort | sed "s|^|#include \"|; s|$|\"|"
+```
+
+The Python CDR decoder needs no action: `src/chf/cdr-decode.py.in` is filled
+from `modified/` at build time, so it cannot drift from the encoder.
+
+Rationale for the trim
+----------------------
+
+`CHFRecord` reaches 353 types across seven sibling charging modules, TS 29.002
+MAP, CAMEL CAP and ITU-T CMIP/ACSE/X.721 — none of which a PDU-session CDR
+needs, and some of which 3GPP does not publish. `closure.py` keeps only what
+the trimmed records reach: 26 types, 21 of them copied verbatim. Because only
+`OPTIONAL` fields were dropped and no tag moved, a decoder built from the
+complete TS 32.298 still reads our records.
+
+The fuller account, including what an R20 upgrade involves, is section 5.2 of
+`docs/CHF-Technical-Overview.md`.
+
 Final check
 ===========
 
diff --git a/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/asn2py.py b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/asn2py.py
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2c65803c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/asn2py.py
@@ -0,0 +1,228 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+#
+# Copyright (C) 2026 by Rami Mohamed <ramrode@gmail.com>
+#
+# This file is part of Open5GS.
+#
+# This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
+# it under the terms of the GNU Affero General Public License as published by
+# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
+# (at your option) any later version.
+#
+# This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
+# but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
+# MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
+# GNU General Public License for more details.
+#
+# You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
+# along with this program.  If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
+"""
+Turn the TS 32.298 ASN.1 module into a schema table for the CDR decoder.
+
+Run at build time, so the decoder's idea of the record comes from the same
+file asn1c generates the C encoder from.  Moving to a newer release means
+re-running generator.sh; the decoder follows without being edited.
+
+The table it emits is deliberately small - just enough to walk a BER
+encoding and name what it finds:
+
+    {"TypeName": {"kind": "SET"|"SEQUENCE"|"CHOICE",
+                  "members": [[tag, "fieldName", "TypeName", is_seq_of], ...]},
+     "TypeName": {"kind": "INTEGER"|"ENUMERATED", "values": {n: "name"}},
+     "TypeName": {"kind": "OCTET STRING"|"IA5String"|"UTF8String"}}
+
+Usage:
+    asn2py.py --asn modified/<module>.asn --template <in> --out <out>
+
+The template is copied through with the line containing the marker
+"@@SCHEMA@@" replaced by the generated table.
+"""
+import argparse
+import re
+import sys
+
+MARKER = "@@SCHEMA@@"
+
+# "fieldName   [12] TypeName OPTIONAL," with any spacing, and the type
+# possibly being "SEQUENCE OF Thing".
+MEMBER_RE = re.compile(
+    r"^\s*([a-zA-Z][\w-]*)\s*"          # field name
+    r"\[(\d+)\]\s*"                     # [tag]
+    r"(SEQUENCE\s+OF\s+)?"              # SEQUENCE OF?
+    r"([A-Za-z][\w-]*(?:\s+STRING)?)"   # type (incl. "OCTET STRING")
+    r"\s*(OPTIONAL)?\s*,?\s*$"
+)
+
+# "name  (12)," inside an INTEGER or ENUMERATED value list.
+VALUE_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*([a-zA-Z][\w-]*)\s*\((-?\d+)\)\s*,?\s*$")
+
+DEF_RE = re.compile(r"^([A-Za-z][\w-]*)\s*::=\s*(.*)$")
+
+STRING_KINDS = ("OCTET STRING", "IA5String", "UTF8String", "GraphicString",
+                "PrintableString", "VisibleString", "NumericString")
+
+
+def strip_comment(line):
+    """Drop an ASN.1 comment. A second '--' closes one, so honour that."""
+    i = line.find("--")
+    if i < 0:
+        return line
+    rest = line[i + 2:]
+    j = rest.find("--")
+    if j >= 0:
+        return line[:i] + rest[j + 2:]
+    return line[:i]
+
+
+def parse(path):
+    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
+        raw = f.read().split("\n")
+
+    lines = [strip_comment(ln) for ln in raw]
+
+    types = {}
+    i = 0
+    while i < len(lines):
+        m = DEF_RE.match(lines[i])
+        if not m:
+            i += 1
+            continue
+
+        name, tail = m.group(1), m.group(2).strip()
+        i += 1
+
+        # Constructed: the body runs to the closing brace at column 0, or
+        # to a lone "}".
+        if tail.startswith(("SET", "SEQUENCE", "CHOICE")) and "OF" not in tail:
+            kind = tail.split()[0]
+            members = []
+            while i < len(lines):
+                ln = lines[i]
+                i += 1
+                if ln.strip().startswith("}"):
+                    break
+                mm = MEMBER_RE.match(ln)
+                if mm:
+                    members.append([
+                        int(mm.group(2)),
+                        mm.group(1),
+                        re.sub(r"\s+", " ", mm.group(4)).strip(),
+                        bool(mm.group(3)),
+                    ])
+            types[name] = {"kind": kind, "members": members}
+            continue
+
+        if tail.startswith(("INTEGER", "ENUMERATED")):
+            kind = "ENUMERATED" if tail.startswith("ENUMERATED") else "INTEGER"
+            values = {}
+
+            # The named-value list may open on this line, or after blank
+            # and comment lines - TS 32.298 puts a paragraph of commentary
+            # between "RecordType ::= INTEGER" and its "{".  Scan forward
+            # for the brace, but stop at the next definition so a type
+            # with no names does not adopt the following type's list.
+            opened = tail.rstrip().endswith("{")
+            if not opened:
+                j = i
+                while j < len(lines):
+                    s = lines[j].strip()
+                    if not s:
+                        j += 1
+                        continue
+                    if s == "{":
+                        opened = True
+                        i = j + 1
+                    break
+
+            if opened:
+                while i < len(lines):
+                    ln = lines[i]
+                    i += 1
+                    if ln.strip().startswith("}"):
+                        break
+                    vm = VALUE_RE.match(ln)
+                    if vm:
+                        values[int(vm.group(2))] = vm.group(1)
+
+            types[name] = {"kind": kind}
+            if values:
+                types[name]["values"] = values
+            continue
+
+        for sk in STRING_KINDS:
+            if tail.startswith(sk):
+                types[name] = {"kind": sk}
+                break
+        else:
+            # A type we do not model: record the kind so the decoder can
+            # say so rather than guess.
+            if tail:
+                types[name] = {"kind": tail.split()[0]}
+
+    return types
+
+
+def emit(types):
+    out = ["SCHEMA = {"]
+    for name in sorted(types):
+        t = types[name]
+        if "members" in t:
+            out.append("    %r: {" % name)
+            out.append("        'kind': %r," % t["kind"])
+            out.append("        'members': [")
+            for tag, field, typ, seqof in t["members"]:
+                out.append("            (%d, %r, %r, %s)," %
+                           (tag, field, typ, seqof))
+            out.append("        ],")
+            out.append("    },")
+        elif "values" in t:
+            out.append("    %r: {'kind': %r, 'values': {%s}}," % (
+                name, t["kind"],
+                ", ".join("%d: %r" % (k, v)
+                          for k, v in sorted(t["values"].items()))))
+        else:
+            out.append("    %r: {'kind': %r}," % (name, t["kind"]))
+    out.append("}")
+    return "\n".join(out)
+
+
+def main():
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    ap.add_argument("--asn", required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--template", required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--out", required=True)
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+
+    types = parse(args.asn)
+    if "CHFRecord" not in types or "ChargingRecord" not in types:
+        sys.stderr.write(
+            "asn2py: %s has no CHFRecord/ChargingRecord - wrong module?\n"
+            % args.asn)
+        return 1
+
+    table = emit(types)
+
+    with open(args.template, encoding="utf-8") as f:
+        template = f.read()
+
+    if MARKER not in template:
+        sys.stderr.write("asn2py: %s has no %s marker\n"
+                         % (args.template, MARKER))
+        return 1
+
+    # Replace the whole line holding the marker.
+    lines = template.split("\n")
+    for n, ln in enumerate(lines):
+        if MARKER in ln:
+            lines[n] = table
+            break
+
+    with open(args.out, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
+        f.write("\n".join(lines))
+
+    sys.stderr.write("asn2py: %d types -> %s\n" % (len(types), args.out))
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main())
diff --git a/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/closure.py b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/closure.py
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6a4f18b8a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/closure.py
@@ -0,0 +1,182 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""
+Compute the transitive type closure of a set of ASN.1 roots across the
+3GPP TS 32.298 modules, and emit one self-contained module.
+
+Why: TS 32.298's CHFChargingDataTypes IMPORTS from seven sibling charging
+modules, which in turn reach TS 29.002 MAP, CAMEL CAP and ITU-T
+CMIP/ACSE/X.721.  Nothing on the 5G SA PDU-session path needs any of that,
+so we take the closure of what the CHF record actually reaches and leave
+the rest out.  Every retained definition is copied verbatim, so tags,
+types and value ranges stay exactly as 3GPP published them.
+"""
+import re
+import sys
+
+DEF_RE = re.compile(r"^([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9-]*)\s*::=")
+# A reference is any upper-case-initial identifier. The lookbehind stops a
+# hyphenated enum value such as "eND-USER-IMSI" from being read as a
+# reference to a type called "USER-IMSI". ASN.1 builtins and keywords are
+# filtered out below.
+REF_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9-]*)\b")
+
+BUILTIN = {
+    "SEQUENCE", "SET", "OF", "CHOICE", "ENUMERATED", "INTEGER", "BOOLEAN",
+    "OCTET", "STRING", "BIT", "NULL", "OPTIONAL", "DEFAULT", "SIZE", "TRUE",
+    "FALSE", "UTF8String", "IA5String", "PrintableString", "VisibleString",
+    "NumericString", "GraphicString", "GeneralString", "TeletexString",
+    "UniversalString", "BMPString", "UTCTime", "GeneralizedTime",
+    "OBJECT", "IDENTIFIER", "ANY", "DEFINED", "BY", "COMPONENTS", "WITH",
+    "FROM", "IMPORTS", "EXPORTS", "BEGIN", "END", "DEFINITIONS", "IMPLICIT",
+    "EXPLICIT", "AUTOMATIC", "TAGS", "APPLICATION", "UNIVERSAL", "PRIVATE",
+    "MIN", "MAX", "ABSENT", "PRESENT", "INCLUDES", "EXCEPT", "ALL",
+    "REAL", "EMBEDDED", "PDV", "EXTERNAL", "RELATIVE-OID", "CLASS",
+    "CONSTRAINED", "ENCODED", "CHARACTER", "ObjectDescriptor",
+}
+
+
+def strip_comments(text):
+    return "\n".join(re.sub(r"--.*$", "", ln) for ln in text.split("\n"))
+
+
+def parse_module(path):
+    """name -> verbatim definition text (comments kept)."""
+    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
+        lines = f.read().split("\n")
+    # Only the body between BEGIN and the final END holds assignments.
+    starts = []
+    for i, ln in enumerate(lines):
+        m = DEF_RE.match(ln)
+        if m:
+            starts.append((i, m.group(1)))
+    defs = {}
+    for idx, (i, name) in enumerate(starts):
+        end = starts[idx + 1][0] if idx + 1 < len(starts) else len(lines)
+        body = lines[i:end]
+        # Trim trailing blank lines and a trailing bare END.
+        while body and (body[-1].strip() == "" or body[-1].strip() == "END"):
+            body.pop()
+        defs[name] = "\n".join(body)
+    return defs
+
+
+def refs_of(text):
+    body = strip_comments(text)
+    # Drop the "Name ::=" head so a definition doesn't reference itself.
+    body = re.sub(r"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9-]*\s*::=", "", body, count=1)
+    out = set()
+    for m in REF_RE.finditer(body):
+        tok = m.group(1)
+        if tok in BUILTIN:
+            continue
+        out.add(tok)
+    return out
+
+
+def module_header(path):
+    """The 3GPP module identifier and DEFINITIONS line, verbatim."""
+    out = []
+    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
+        for ln in f:
+            out.append(ln.rstrip("\n"))
+            if ln.strip() == "BEGIN":
+                break
+            if len(out) > 20:            # header is a handful of lines
+                break
+    # Everything up to BEGIN, minus any IMPORTS (there are none to keep).
+    keep = []
+    for ln in out:
+        if ln.strip().startswith("IMPORTS"):
+            break
+        keep.append(ln)
+    if not any(l.strip() == "BEGIN" for l in keep):
+        keep.append("")
+        keep.append("BEGIN")
+    return "\n".join(keep)
+
+
+def main():
+    roots = []
+    paths = []
+    overrides = []
+    emit_from = None
+    mode = None
+    for a in sys.argv[1:]:
+        if a == "--root":
+            mode = "root"
+        elif a == "--override":
+            mode = "override"
+        elif a == "--module":
+            mode = "module"
+        elif a == "--emit-module":
+            mode = "emit"
+        elif mode == "root":
+            roots.append(a)
+        elif mode == "override":
+            overrides.append(a)
+        elif mode == "module":
+            paths.append(a)
+        elif mode == "emit":
+            emit_from = a
+
+    defs = {}
+    provenance = {}
+    for p in paths:
+        for k, v in parse_module(p).items():
+            if k not in defs:          # first module wins
+                defs[k] = v
+                provenance[k] = p.split("/")[-1]
+
+    # Overrides replace a 3GPP definition with our trimmed one.
+    for p in overrides:
+        for k, v in parse_module(p).items():
+            defs[k] = v
+            provenance[k] = "(trimmed) " + p.split("/")[-1]
+
+    seen = set()
+    missing = {}
+    order = []
+    stack = list(roots)
+    while stack:
+        name = stack.pop()
+        if name in seen:
+            continue
+        if name not in defs:
+            missing.setdefault(name, set())
+            continue
+        seen.add(name)
+        order.append(name)
+        for r in sorted(refs_of(defs[name])):
+            if r not in seen:
+                stack.append(r)
+            if r not in defs:
+                missing.setdefault(r, set()).add(name)
+
+    sys.stderr.write("closure: %d types from %d roots\n" % (len(order), len(roots)))
+    if missing:
+        sys.stderr.write("UNRESOLVED (%d):\n" % len(missing))
+        for k in sorted(missing):
+            sys.stderr.write("  %-40s <- %s\n" % (k, ", ".join(sorted(missing[k])) or "root"))
+
+    if emit_from:
+        # A second "--" on a line closes an ASN.1 comment, so the text of
+        # these must not contain one.
+        print("-- Generated by closure.py. Do not edit.")
+        print("-- Self-contained 5G SA subset of 3GPP TS 32.298 CHF CDRs.")
+        print("-- Definitions marked (trimmed) come from patched/; every other")
+        print("-- definition is copied verbatim from standard/.")
+        print()
+        print(module_header(emit_from))
+        print()
+
+    for name in sorted(order):
+        print("-- [%s]" % provenance[name])
+        print(defs[name])
+        print()
+
+    if emit_from:
+        print("END")
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
diff --git a/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/generator.sh b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/generator.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..27f07cf97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/asn1c/support/cdr-r19.6.0/generator.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+#
+# Regenerate the TS 32.298 CHF CDR ASN.1 encoder/decoder.
+#
+#   standard/  pristine 3GPP modules, exactly as published on 3GPP Forge
+#   patched/   the only hand-written ASN.1: the records trimmed to 5G SA,
+#              plus corrections for defects in the published module
+#   closure.py standard + patched -> modified/  (a self-contained module)
+#   modified/  the asn1c input, committed so review can read it
+#   asn1c      modified/ -> lib/asn1c/cdr/
+#
+# Usage:
+#   ASN1C=/path/to/asn1c/asn1c/asn1c ./generator.sh
+#
+# See ../README.md ("Regenerate the CHF CDR ASN.1 files") for how to build
+# asn1c and which commit to use.
+#
+set -e
+
+HERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
+OUT=$(cd "$HERE/../../cdr" 2>/dev/null && pwd) || OUT="$HERE/../../cdr"
+
+ASN1C=${ASN1C:-asn1c}
+if ! command -v "$ASN1C" > /dev/null 2>&1 && [ ! -x "$ASN1C" ]; then
+    echo "error: asn1c not found. Set ASN1C=/path/to/asn1c/asn1c/asn1c" >&2
+    exit 1
+fi
+
+MODULE=32298-j60-chf-5gsa.asn
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+# 1. standard/ + patched/ -> modified/
+#
+# The CHF record reaches 353 types across seven sibling charging modules,
+# TS 29.002 MAP, CAMEL CAP and ITU-T CMIP/ACSE/X.721.  Nothing on the 5G SA
+# PDU-session path needs any of it, so closure.py keeps only what the
+# trimmed records actually reach - 26 types, of which 21 are copied
+# verbatim from standard/.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+echo "closure: standard/ + patched/ -> modified/$MODULE"
+python3 "$HERE/closure.py" \
+    --root CHFRecord \
+    --module "$HERE/standard/TS32298_CHFChargingDataTypes.asn" \
+             "$HERE/standard/TS32298_GenericChargingDataTypes.asn" \
+             "$HERE/standard/TS32298_GPRSChargingDataTypes.asn" \
+    --override "$HERE/patched/chf-5gsa-records.asn" \
+               "$HERE/patched/spec-defects.asn" \
+    --emit-module "$HERE/standard/TS32298_CHFChargingDataTypes.asn" \
+    > "$HERE/modified/$MODULE"
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+# 2. modified/ -> lib/asn1c/cdr/
+#
+# BER is the one encoding kept: TS 32.298 clause 6.1 requires it on Bx
+# ("Data Record Format" 1).  asn1c's encoder emits DER, which is a
+# canonical subset of BER, so any BER decoder reads what we write.
+#
+# NGAP and S1AP are generated with -no-gen-BER and keep APER instead; the
+# CDR codec is the mirror image, so it cannot share their runtime.  See
+# ../../cdr/meson.build.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+echo "asn1c: modified/$MODULE -> $OUT"
+mkdir -p "$OUT"
+cd "$OUT"
+"$ASN1C" -pdu=all \
+    -fprefix=CHFCDR_ -fcompound-names -findirect-choice -fno-include-deps \
+    -no-gen-XER -no-gen-JER -no-gen-CBOR \
+    -no-gen-OER -no-gen-UPER -no-gen-APER \
+    -no-gen-random-fill -no-gen-example \
+    "$HERE/modified/$MODULE"
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+# 3. Drop the fragments asn1c leaves behind
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+rm -f Makefile.am.asn1convert Makefile.am.libasncodec \
+      converter-example.mk converter-example.c pdu_collection.c
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+# 4. Route allocation through ogs_malloc
+#
+# asn_internal.h is the one skeleton open5gs modifies (see ../README.md).
+# lib/asn1c/common already carries the patched form of the same file, so
+# we copy it rather than re-deriving the patch here, and keep the patch
+# itself in one place.
+#
+# This directory deliberately keeps its own full copy of the asn1c
+# runtime instead of sharing lib/asn1c/common.  asn_config.h is written
+# by asn1c from the -no-gen-* flags above, so common's copy has BER off
+# and this one has it on - and a C quote-include resolves against the
+# including file's own directory first.  Sharing common's sources would
+# therefore compile them against common's asn_config.h, giving the shared
+# runtime and the generated code two different layouts for
+# asn_TYPE_operation_s.  That mismatch links cleanly and crashes later,
+# so the duplication buys a real guarantee.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+COMMON="$HERE/../../common"
+
+if ! grep -q "modified by acetcom" "$COMMON/asn_internal.h" 2>/dev/null; then
+    echo "error: $COMMON/asn_internal.h is not the open5gs-patched copy." >&2
+    echo "       Re-check the allocator wrappers before trusting this build." >&2
+    exit 1
+fi
+cp "$COMMON/asn_internal.h" "$OUT/asn_internal.h"
+
+echo
+echo "Generated $(ls "$OUT" | grep -c '\.c$') .c and $(ls "$OUT" | grep -c '\.h$') .h files."
+
+# Everything else asn1c copied should be the stock skeleton. Point out
+# any that drifted from common's, so a release bump does not slip past.
+drifted=""
+for f in "$OUT"/*.c "$OUT"/*.h; do
+    b=$(basename "$f")
+    case "$b" in CHFCDR_*|asn_config.h|asn_internal.h) continue ;; esac
+    [ -f "$COMMON/$b" ] || continue
+    cmp -s "$f" "$COMMON/$b" || drifted="$drifted $b"
+done
+if [ -n "$drifted" ]; then
+    echo
+    echo "These skeletons differ from lib/asn1c/common - check whether that is"
+    echo "an asn1c version difference before committing:"
+    for b in $drifted; do echo "  $b"; done
+fi
+
+echo
+echo "Now sync the source list in $OUT/meson.build and the header list in"
+echo "lib/asn1c/cdr/ogs-asn1c-cdr.h by hand - neither is generated."
